From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:08:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/52] Fix truth value of KiCad colors

Color.__bool__ returned the first non-zero channel instead of a bool, so
bool() raised a TypeError for colors with a non-zero channel, which broke
the SVG export of anything with a colored stroke.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013wvKon1yvwjNtAdtSuZzZh
---
 src/gerbonara/cad/kicad/base_types.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gerbonara/cad/kicad/base_types.py b/src/gerbonara/cad/kicad/base_types.py
index f794ea9..30079e5 100644
--- a/src/gerbonara/cad/kicad/base_types.py
+++ b/src/gerbonara/cad/kicad/base_types.py
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@ class Color:
     a: float = None
     
     def __bool__(self):
-        return self.r or self.b or self.g or not math.isclose(self.a, 0, abs_tol=1e-3)
+        return bool(self.r or self.b or self.g or not math.isclose(self.a or 0, 0, abs_tol=1e-3))
 
     def svg(self, default=None):
         if default and not self:
